---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Support — Paw Watch"
  description="Get help with Paw Watch. Contact us, read FAQs, and find resources."
>
  <section class="wrap-narrow prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most questions are answered below. If you're stuck, email us and
      we'll get back to you within two business days.
    </p>

    <div class="card contact-card">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <dl class="contact">
        <dt>Email</dt>
        <dd><a href="mailto:support@paw-watch.app">support@paw-watch.app</a></dd>
        <dt>Response time</dt>
        <dd>Within 2 business days</dd>
        <dt>Privacy questions</dt>
        <dd><a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
      <p>
        Open the Profile tab, tap <strong>Account</strong>, scroll to
        the bottom, and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>. You'll be
        asked to type the word "delete" to confirm. Your profile,
        reports, walks, pets, alert history, and notification tokens
        are removed immediately — there's no 30-day waiting period.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you no longer have access to the app, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a>
        from the address you signed up with and we'll delete your
        account within 30 days.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>How do I report a hazard?</h3>
      <p>
        Open Paw Watch, tap the red <strong>+ Report</strong> button at
        the bottom of the map, pick a category, set the severity, and
        add a short description. Most reports take under 30 seconds.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Why aren't I getting push notifications?</h3>
      <p>
        Three things to check:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You granted notification permission to Paw Watch (iOS Settings
          → Paw Watch → Notifications).
        </li>
        <li>
          Your home radius is set and your alert categories are enabled
          (Profile tab → Alerts).
        </li>
        <li>
          You have a working internet connection. Try opening the map
          to confirm.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Still stuck? Email
        <a href="mailto:support@paw-watch.app">support@paw-watch.app</a>
        and we'll help you debug.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Why is my report missing from the map?</h3>
      <p>
        Reports expire based on severity: low (24h), medium (72h),
        high (7d). After that, the row is deleted from our database —
        not just hidden. If you just submitted it and don't see it,
        try pulling down to refresh the map.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Can I use Paw Watch without sharing my location?</h3>
      <p>
        You can browse the map and read reports without granting
        location. You'll need to grant location to submit reports and
        to receive alerts. To turn off location later, go to iOS
        Settings → Paw Watch → Location.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Why was my report downgraded or hidden?</h3>
      <p>
        If multiple walkers report the same hazard as no longer
        present, or if multiple walkers disagree with the report,
        Paw Watch will auto-deactivate it. We surface the dispute
        count on the report's detail page so you can see the
        breakdown.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>How do I flag a report or block a user?</h3>
      <p>
        Open any hazard report and tap <strong>Report this content</strong>
        at the bottom. You can choose a category (harassment, hate
        speech, off-topic, impersonation, or other) and add an optional
        note. Flagged reports are reviewed by a moderator within 24 hours.
      </p>
      <p>
        To block a walker entirely, open any of their reports and tap
        <strong>Block this user</strong> at the bottom. You'll be asked
        to type the word "block" to confirm. Their reports will no
        longer appear on your map, and you can unblock from
        <strong>Profile → Blocked users</strong> at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use an automated moderation service to scan new reports
        before they appear on the map, and a 24-hour SLA guarantees
        that flagged reports are removed within one day. The full
        operational runbook is published at
        <a href="https://github.com/cerminaraconsulting/pawwatch/blob/main/docs/ugc-moderation-runbook.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/cerminaraconsulting/pawwatch/docs/ugc-moderation-runbook.md</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>How do I invite a walker to walk my dog?</h3>
      <p>
        Open the Profile tab, tap "Invites," and tap "Send invite."
        They'll get a 6-character code (also available as a QR code)
        that they can enter when they sign up. Your roles will update
        automatically when they accept.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>App version</h3>
      <p>
        Paw Watch 1.0 (build 1). Built with Expo and React Native.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 2em;
  }
  .contact-card {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #fef7f1 0%, #ffffff 100%);
  }
  .card h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .card ul {
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }
</style>
